           First reproduce the reported behavior with the smallest relevant test or command. Implement the minimal fix, run the focused regression test, then run adjacent tests and inspect failures. If any validation fails, diagnose and revise the patch rather than submitting; only finish after confirming both the regression and relevant existing behavior.
           For every behavior change, write an edge-case matrix before coding: normal, empty or missing, invalid, boundary, repeated, and backward-compatible inputs. Derive expected outcomes from repository conventions, nearby implementations, and existing tests rather than inventing new semantics.
